unty, Maine.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00\", \"start\": 308, \"end\": 413, \"text\": \"He resided in the Nathaniel Treat House, which is now listed on the National Register of Historic Places.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00\", \"start\": 414, \"end\": 481, \"text\": \"Dunn was involved with the Merrill Trust and Orono Trust Companies.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00\", \"start\": 482, \"end\": 531, \"text\": \"He was also treasurer of the University of Maine.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00\", \"start\": 532, \"end\": 589, \"text\": \"He served in the Maine House of Representatives from 1901\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 1, \"text\": \".\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d01\", \"start\": 2, \"end\": 73, \"text\": \"Wikipedia® is a registered trademark of the Wikimedia Foundation , Inc.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d01\", \"start\": 74, \"end\": 103, \"text\": \", a non-profit organization .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d01\", \"start\": 104, \"end\": 334, \"text\": \"Privacy policy About Wikipedia Disclaimers Contact Wikipedia Code of Conduct Developers Statistics Cookie statement Mobile view Search Search Toggle the table of contents Charles Dunn ( Wisconsin politician ) 2 languages Add topic\"}}, \"candidates\": [{\"candidate_id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Houghton County, Michigan\", \"card_ids\": [\"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00:c0\"]}], \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0029-984204398011:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Justice Dunn\", \"scope\": \"Birthplace\", \"claim\": \"Justice Dunn was